{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1091464-data-sphere-seems-too-slow-advice-needed","id":1091464,"title":"Data sphere seems too slow; advice needed.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-12T02:11:50-07:00","id":1091464,"title":"Data sphere seems too slow; advice needed.","content":"The main mechanical difference between spheres of Data and Correspondence, in our group understanding, is that Data doesn't require successes for range; instead, before affecting a given target for the first time, character collates data on it by means of extended Enigmas roll.<br /> The problem is, the data collation process is quite slow until mage achieves mastery in Data sphere. Our Data specialist has 3rd level in the sphere, which means that he get to roll once per hour for collating data on each new target. Sure, after the data is ready, he will not need additional successes to affect the target compared to Correspondence mage. However, additional successes means at most brief rite for Correspondence mage (five minutes or less if using Rite, Ceremony and Great Work optional rule), while Data mage, gathering intel on several new targets, must spend at least a hour preparing for each effect, more with some unlucky rolls. Combined with other disadvantages (no use for targets &quot;off the grid&quot;, doesn't work in Umbra), Data sphere looks rather weak compared to Correspondence - at least for starting character.<br /> Are we missing something, or if not, how would you advice to fix the balance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","name":"mindszenty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T21:35:13-07:00","id":1091824,"title":"","content":"Well for one, you're missing that Correspondence users have to establish Sympathetic connections. With Data, the information you need is all out there, on the web. The time collating information is the process of getting it all together to establish your connection. If you're using Correspondence, you have to go out and establish the connection yourself.<br /> <br /> This means one of two things: 1) finding items or body samples that are tied to the target by way of the Rule of Contagion, or 2) making yourself connected to the target through personal interaction. This means either tracking down things like personal belongings or hair or blood, or meeting the target and getting to know them. The stronger the connection (and thereby the fewer successes you need to roll to connect to them), the more particular those items or the stronger the relationship that must be.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the heart of the matter. If you're breaking into the target's house to steal a personal possession, for example, is that significantly easier or less time consuming that crunching some numbers on the net? If you're making making yourself well-known enough to the target that they would consider you a significant acquintence (if not friend), is that a superior method to information collating?<br /> <br /> Let's just say that if I'm stalking a guy long enough to find his barber, then sneaking in to grab bits of his hair clippings, in the interests of pulling magic on him...am I really so much better off than a VA or NWO agent who trawls the person's Facebook account for a couple hours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T10:19:14-07:00","id":1091996,"title":"","content":"Thank you for pointing this out. However, I am not missing the need for sympathetic connection; but I may underestimate its impact. The additional successes I mentioned Correspondence mage will need are exactly for lack of close sympathetic connection with a target. Now, if a mage have absolutely no sympathetic connection to a target character, then they require six or more successes on the effect roll - how much more, and what this number depends on, the rules do not say. If <i>Rite, Ceremony and Great Work</i> rule is used, this places effect at least in Ceremony range and comparable time-frame with 3rd level Data collation. However, &quot;briefly touched or met object or person&quot; degree of connection requires only five successes, and fall within that possible with a brief five-minutes rite. &quot;Described location&quot; also requires same five successes. One could say, then, that even such fleeting degree of sympathetic connection requires, on average, more than a hour of time to establish (e.g. to obtain a cup from which target drank in a cafe is simpler than one of their personal possession, but still an effort).<br /> <br /> However, I feel there are still situations when Correspondence has a upper hand, but this may be within intended balance. E.g. compare Correspondence Landscape of the Mind with Data Sousveillance to sense what happens behind the wall. I feel this counts as &quot;Line of Sight&quot; range for Correspondence, one success worth (I may be wrong here, of course). On the other hand, Data mage still needs a hour for data collation, if they sets up the sousveillance for the first time for given location. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","name":"mindszenty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:04:02-07:00","id":1092031,"title":"","content":"Data's &quot;canonical&quot; but it suffers from what I consider to be typical flaws of fan-designed alternative Spheres in that it oscillates between being Crazy Good and Kind of Terrible and its supposed tradeoffs and weaknesses can be read in inconsistent ways with radically different outcomes. My recommendations would be something like: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Ignore Data's Enigmas minigame and instead consider it an alternate Correspondence range chart. Staple the Range Chart onto it, because losing that isn't actually a benefit. Data users can, like Corr users, always attempt to use a more remote link that requires more successes, regardless of Sphere level.</li> <li>Being &quot;on the grid&quot; is irrelevant except for considerations of vulgarity.</li> <li>Data may &quot;act as&quot; Forces or Entropy when manipulating electronic data.</li> <li>Data cannot be used in the Umbra or in other Realms without conjunctional Dimensional Science to amend coordinates. (Data will also, but not as a rule, have trouble targeting umbrood and other beings, because data links to them are usually nonexistent.)</li> <li>Corr and Data may ward and defend against one another, and can be used to break sympathetic or data links, with some limits:</li> <li>Corr can sever a data link by acting on an original &quot;seed&quot; data (any number of copies will be affected sympathetically) but cannot target most digital links without conjunctional Forces.</li> <li>Corr-based disruption of a copy of seed data doesn't affect the original; it only works one-way.</li> <li>Data cannot use Chain, the three-dot Corr effect, but Data 3 users can use copies of seed data in place of the original. This means that an original data source can be placed in a secure location while disciples of Data can use copies that are less vulnerable and can be replaced if destroyed.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T22:52:52-07:00","id":1092244,"title":"","content":"Personally I always preferred Void Correspondence for my Technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:46:34-07:00","id":1093382,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, Five Eyes, these are really helpful suggestions! I was thinking about changing data sympathy to just range, but others points are, too, very interesting.<br /> Enginseer-42, thanks for bringing up Void Correspondence, I almost forgot about it! However, for now we have an traditionalist cabal, and the Data specialist in question is Virtual Adept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","name":"mindszenty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T23:57:56-07:00","id":1093554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mindszenty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1091464-data-sphere-seems-too-slow-advice-needed?p=1093382#post1093382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, for now we have an traditionalist cabal</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't subsribe under any ideology and act, as a sovereign entity in most interactions, so thank you, but I'm not a &quot;traditionalist&quot;!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T14:57:54-07:00","id":1093840,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Well, I oversimplified things. But certainly not a Technocratic Amalgam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","name":"mindszenty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}